.Dd November 23, 2026
.Dt MDFIND 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm mdfind
.Nd find files by their metadata
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl count
.Op Fl 0
.Op Fl attr Ar attribute
.Op Fl onlyin Ar directory ...
.Fl name Ar name | Ar query
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
lists the files that match
.Ar query .
There is no metadata index yet: the files are searched on the disk, under
the
.Fl onlyin
directories or, by default, the user's home folder,
.Pa /Applications
and
.Pa /System/Applications .
Invisible files are skipped; a package (an application) is one file.
.Pp
A query of words finds the files whose name, or text for a text file,
has every word, whatever their case.
An expression compares attributes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kMDItemFSName == '*.txt'c
kMDItemContentTypeTree == 'public.image'
kMDItemFSSize > 1000000 && kMDItemFSContentChangeDate >= $time.today(-7)
.Ed
.Pp
Values in quotes may have
.Ql *
wildcards and be followed by
.Cm c
(any case),
.Cm d
(any diacritics) or
.Cm w
(a word).
Numbers and dates compare with
.Ql < > <= >= ;
dates are
.Cm $time.now ,
.Cm $time.today ,
.Cm $time.today( Ns Ar days Ns Cm ) ,
.Cm $time.iso( Ns Ar date Ns Cm ) .
Expressions join with
.Ql && ,
.Ql || ,
.Ql \&!
and parentheses.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl name Ar name
Files whose name has
.Ar name .
.It Fl onlyin Ar directory
Search only there (the option may be repeated).
.It Fl count
Only the number of files found.
.It Fl attr Ar attribute
Each file's value of the attribute, after its path.
.It Fl 0
NUL characters between the paths.
.El
.Pp
.Fl live
and
.Fl s
need the index and are refused.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mdls 1 ,
.Xr mdutil 1
